---
// src/pages/nostr.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Layout title="Intro to Nostr" description="A layman's guide to Nostr — the open, censorship-resistant social protocol.">
  <main class="nostr-root">

    <!-- ── HERO ── -->
    <section class="nostr-hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-tag">
          <span class="ping-dot"></span>
          Protocol · Decentralisation · Open Web
        </div>
        <h1>
          <span class="hero-sub">What is</span>
          Nostr
          <span class="mark">?</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-desc">
          A dead-simple, unstoppable protocol for social media and beyond —
          no company owns it, no server can silence you, and anyone can build on it.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-jump-links">
          <a href="#what" class="jump">What it is</a>
          <a href="#how" class="jump">How it works</a>
          <a href="#why" class="jump">Why it matters</a>
          <a href="#start" class="jump">Get started</a>
          <a href="#resources" class="jump">Resources</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg class="relay-diagram" viewBox="0 0 320 320" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <!-- relay rings -->
          <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="130" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.07)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="90"  stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.10)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="50"  stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.14)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <!-- spoke lines -->
          <line x1="160" y1="160" x2="160" y2="30"  stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.18)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
          <line x1="160" y1="160" x2="275" y2="227" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.18)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
          <line x1="160" y1="160" x2="45"  y2="227" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.18)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
          <line x1="160" y1="160" x2="290" y2="100" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.10)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
          <line x1="160" y1="160" x2="30"  y2="100" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.10)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
          <line x1="160" y1="160" x2="160" y2="290" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.10)" stroke-width="0.75" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>
          <!-- outer relay nodes -->
          <circle cx="160" cy="30"  r="7" fill="#0d1519" stroke="#2a7a60" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="275" cy="227" r="7" fill="#0d1519" stroke="#2a7a60" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="45"  cy="227" r="7" fill="#0d1519" stroke="#2a7a60" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="290" cy="100" r="5" fill="#0d1519" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <circle cx="30"  cy="100" r="5" fill="#0d1519" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <circle cx="160" cy="290" r="5" fill="#0d1519" stroke="rgba(72,201,160,0.3)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <!-- relay labels -->
          <text x="160" y="17"  text-anchor="middle" font-family="JetBrains Mono,monospace" font-size="7" fill="rgba(72,201,160,0.55)">relay</text>
          <text x="287" y="243" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JetBrains Mono,monospace" font-size="7" fill="rgba(72,201,160,0.55)">relay</text>
          <text x="33"  y="243" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JetBrains Mono,monospace" font-size="7" fill="rgba(72,201,160,0.55)">relay</text>
          <!-- centre user node -->
          <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="18" fill="rgba(72,201,160,0.08)" stroke="#48c9a0" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="160" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-family="JetBrains Mono,monospace" font-size="8" fill="#48c9a0">you</text>
          <!-- animated pulse ring -->
          <circle cx="160" cy="160" r="18" fill="none" stroke="#48c9a0" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.6">
            <animate attributeName="r" values="18;42;18" dur="3s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
            <animate attributeName="opacity" values="0.6;0;0.6" dur="3s" repeatCount="indefinite"/>
          </circle>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── WHAT ── -->
    <div class="chart-divider"><span class="chart-divider-label">What is Nostr</span></div>
    <section id="what" class="content-section reveal">
      <div class="section-label">Synopsis</div>
      <div class="two-col">
        <div class="prose-block">
          <p>
            <strong>Nostr</strong> stands for <em>Notes and Other Stuff Transmitted by Relays</em>.
            It is a bare-bones open protocol — essentially a shared language that any app,
            server, or person can speak — for publishing and reading short messages on the internet.
          </p>
          <p>
            Think of it like email, but for social media. No single company runs email —
            Gmail, Outlook and your work server all talk to each other using the same rules.
            Nostr applies that same logic to posts, follows, likes, and direct messages.
          </p>
          <p>
            The result: you own your identity and your content. There is no Geoffrey-West.social
            that can ban you, no algorithm deciding what you see, and no data centre whose
            shutdown takes everything offline.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="callout-stack">
          <div class="callout callout--green">
            <div class="callout-label">// in one sentence</div>
            <p>Nostr is an open protocol that lets anyone publish signed messages to any server, readable by any app, controlled by no one.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="callout callout--amber">
            <div class="callout-label">// not a blockchain</div>
            <p>No tokens, no mining, no consensus. Just cryptographic keys and simple servers called relays.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── HOW ── -->
    <div class="chart-divider"><span class="chart-divider-label">How It Works</span></div>
    <section id="how" class="content-section reveal">
      <div class="section-label">The Mechanics</div>

      <div class="concept-grid">
        <div class="concept-card">
          <div class="concept-icon">🔑</div>
          <div class="concept-label">// your identity</div>
          <h3>Keypair</h3>
          <p>
            When you join Nostr you generate a <strong>public key</strong> (your username, shareable)
            and a <strong>private key</strong> (your password, never share it).
            Your public key <em>is</em> your identity — no email, no phone number required.
          </p>
          <div class="concept-example">
            <span class="ex-label">public key (npub)</span>
            <code>npub1sg6p…xhv7</code>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="concept-card">
          <div class="concept-icon">📡</div>
          <div class="concept-label">// the servers</div>
          <h3>Relays</h3>
          <p>
            Relays are simple servers that store and forward your messages. They don't interpret
            content — they just hold signed events. You connect to as many or as few as you like.
            If one relay goes down or bans you, your content lives on the others.
          </p>
          <div class="concept-example">
            <span class="ex-label">example relay</span>
            <code>wss://relay.damus.io</code>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="concept-card">
          <div class="concept-icon">✍️</div>
          <div class="concept-label">// the messages</div>
          <h3>Events</h3>
          <p>
            Everything on Nostr is an <strong>event</strong> — a small JSON object containing
            your message, a timestamp, your public key, and a cryptographic signature.
            The signature proves the message is genuinely from you, without needing a central
            authority to vouch for it.
          </p>
          <div class="concept-example">
            <span class="ex-label">event kinds include</span>
            <code>text note · DM · reaction · article</code>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="concept-card">
          <div class="concept-icon">📱</div>
          <div class="concept-label">// the interface</div>
          <h3>Clients</h3>
          <p>
            A client is the app you use to read and write to Nostr — like Damus on iOS,
            Amethyst on Android, or Primal on the web. Because the protocol is open,
            dozens of clients exist. You can switch between them at any time and your
            identity and follows come with you.
          </p>
          <div class="concept-example">
            <span class="ex-label">popular clients</span>
            <code>Damus · Primal · Amethyst · Snort</code>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- flow diagram -->
      <div class="flow-wrap reveal">
        <div class="flow-label">// how a post travels</div>
        <div class="flow">
          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-icon">👤</div>
            <div class="flow-name">You write a note</div>
            <div class="flow-detail">Signed with your private key</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-icon">📡</div>
            <div class="flow-name">Sent to relays</div>
            <div class="flow-detail">One or many servers store it</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-icon">📱</div>
            <div class="flow-name">Clients fetch it</div>
            <div class="flow-detail">Any app can read any relay</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <div class="flow-icon">👥</div>
            <div class="flow-name">Your followers see it</div>
            <div class="flow-detail">No algorithm — chronological</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── WHY ── -->
    <div class="chart-divider"><span class="chart-divider-label">Why It Matters</span></div>
    <section id="why" class="content-section reveal">
      <div class="section-label">The Case for Nostr</div>
      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why-item">
          <div class="why-icon amber">⚓</div>
          <h3>Censorship resistance</h3>
          <p>No single relay or client controls the network. Getting banned from one relay
          is like being kicked out of one coffee shop — every other one still serves you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <div class="why-icon green">🔐</div>
          <h3>Self-sovereign identity</h3>
          <p>Your keypair is your account. You can take it to any client, any relay,
          forever. No platform can delete your identity — only you hold the private key.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <div class="why-icon amber">🌐</div>
          <h3>Open ecosystem</h3>
          <p>Because the protocol is public, anyone can build on it. The result is an
          explosion of apps — social feeds, marketplaces, live streaming, Git hosting,
          and more — all sharing the same identity layer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <div class="why-icon green">⚡</div>
          <h3>Native Lightning payments</h3>
          <p>Nostr was built alongside Bitcoin's Lightning Network. Zapping —
          sending small Bitcoin tips directly to a creator — is built into the
          protocol itself. No payment processor required.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <div class="why-icon amber">👁️</div>
          <h3>No algorithmic feed</h3>
          <p>You see what you follow, in order. There is no engagement-maximising
          algorithm deciding what outrages you most. The feed is yours to curate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <div class="why-icon green">🔓</div>
          <h3>No walled garden</h3>
          <p>Your followers, your posts, your DMs — none of it is locked to one app.
          Switch clients the way you switch email providers. Everything comes with you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── COMPARE ── -->
    <div class="chart-divider"><span class="chart-divider-label">Nostr vs the Alternatives</span></div>
    <section class="content-section reveal">
      <div class="section-label">Comparison</div>
      <div class="compare-table-wrap">
        <table class="compare-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th></th>
              <th class="th-nostr">Nostr</th>
              <th>Twitter / X</th>
              <th>Mastodon</th>
              <th>Bluesky</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="row-label">Identity ownership</td>
              <td class="td-nostr">✦ Your keypair</td>
              <td>✗ Platform</td>
              <td>~ Instance server</td>
              <td>~ DNS handle</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="row-label">Censorship resistance</td>
              <td class="td-nostr">✦ High</td>
              <td>✗ Low</td>
              <td>~ Medium</td>
              <td>~ Medium</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="row-label">Native payments</td>
              <td class="td-nostr">✦ Lightning zaps</td>
              <td>✗ None</td>
              <td>✗ None</td>
              <td>✗ None</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="row-label">Algorithm-free feed</td>
              <td class="td-nostr">✦ Yes</td>
              <td>✗ No</td>
              <td>✦ Yes</td>
              <td>✦ Yes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="row-label">Open protocol</td>
              <td class="td-nostr">✦ Yes (NIPs)</td>
              <td>✗ No</td>
              <td>✦ ActivityPub</td>
              <td>~ AT Protocol</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="row-label">Requires account signup</td>
              <td class="td-nostr">✦ No</td>
              <td>✗ Yes</td>
              <td>✗ Yes</td>
              <td>✗ Yes</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="table-note">✦ = advantage &nbsp;·&nbsp; ~ = partial &nbsp;·&nbsp; ✗ = disadvantage</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── GET STARTED ── -->
    <div class="chart-divider"><span class="chart-divider-label">Getting Started</span></div>
    <section id="start" class="content-section reveal">
      <div class="section-label">First Steps</div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">01</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Pick a client</h3>
            <p>Download an app that speaks Nostr. For beginners, <strong>Primal</strong> (web &amp; mobile)
            or <strong>Damus</strong> (iOS) are the friendliest starting points. The client will
            generate your keys for you on first launch.</p>
            <div class="step-links">
              <a href="https://primal.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="step-link">primal.net →</a>
              <a href="https://damus.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="step-link">damus.io →</a>
              <a href="https://amethyst.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="step-link">amethyst.social →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">02</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Back up your private key</h3>
            <p>Your <code>nsec1…</code> private key is your entire identity. Write it down on
            paper and store it safely. If you lose it, you lose your account — permanently.
            There is no "forgot password".</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">03</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Add some relays</h3>
            <p>Your client will connect to a default set of relays automatically. To improve
            reach and redundancy, add a few more from the public list at
            <a href="https://nostr.watch" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nostr.watch</a>.
            Aim for 5–10 reliable relays.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">04</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Find people to follow</h3>
            <p>Search by <code>npub</code> or by NIP-05 verified username (formatted like an email address:
            <code>geoffrey@thegwjw.com</code>). Follow a few accounts in your field — the feed
            fills up quickly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step-num">05</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Enable zaps (optional)</h3>
            <p>To send and receive Lightning tips, connect a Lightning wallet that supports
            LNURL — Wallet of Satoshi or Alby are the most common choices.
            Set your Lightning address in your profile and you can start receiving zaps.</p>
            <div class="step-links">
              <a href="https://getalby.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="step-link">Alby wallet →</a>
              <a href="https://www.walletofsatoshi.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="step-link">Wallet of Satoshi →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── RESOURCES ── -->
    <div class="chart-divider"><span class="chart-divider-label">Resources</span></div>
    <section id="resources" class="content-section reveal">
      <div class="section-label">Further Reading</div>
      <div class="resource-grid">

        <div class="resource-group">
          <div class="resource-group-title">// official &amp; foundational</div>
          <ul class="resource-list">
            <li>
              <a href="https://github.com/nostr-protocol/nostr" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">nostr-protocol/nostr</span>
                <span class="res-desc">The original GitHub repository — the protocol spec in plain English</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://github.com/nostr-protocol/nips" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">NIPs (Nostr Implementation Possibilities)</span>
                <span class="res-desc">All protocol extensions, from basic posts to marketplaces and live events</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://nostr.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">nostr.com</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Community landing page with an overview and client directory</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-group">
          <div class="resource-group-title">// beginner guides</div>
          <ul class="resource-list">
            <li>
              <a href="https://nostr.how" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">nostr.how</span>
                <span class="res-desc">The friendliest getting-started guide on the internet for Nostr</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://usenostr.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">usenostr.org</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Step-by-step walkthroughs for non-technical users</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.heynostr.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">heynostr.com</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Plain-language explainer aimed at complete newcomers</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-group">
          <div class="resource-group-title">// clients to try</div>
          <ul class="resource-list">
            <li>
              <a href="https://primal.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">Primal</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Web &amp; mobile — the cleanest onboarding experience, includes a built-in wallet</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://damus.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">Damus</span>
                <span class="res-desc">iOS — the original popular Nostr client, started the zaps ecosystem</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://amethyst.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">Amethyst</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Android — feature-rich with relay management and zap support</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://snort.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">Snort</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Web — fast, minimal, good for power users</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-group">
          <div class="resource-group-title">// tools &amp; infrastructure</div>
          <ul class="resource-list">
            <li>
              <a href="https://nostr.watch" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">nostr.watch</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Live map and status of public relays worldwide</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://njump.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">njump.me</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Web gateway — view any Nostr profile or note without an account</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://getalby.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">Alby</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Browser extension wallet — simplest way to enable zaps in web clients</span>
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://nostr.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="resource-link">
                <span class="res-title">nostr.build</span>
                <span class="res-desc">Free media hosting for images and video on Nostr</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── FAQ ── -->
    <div class="chart-divider"><span class="chart-divider-label">Common Questions</span></div>
    <section class="content-section reveal">
      <div class="section-label">FAQ</div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Is Nostr anonymous?</summary>
          <p class="faq-a">By default your identity is a public key with no name attached — pseudonymous rather than anonymous. You can share as much or as little personal information as you choose. For stronger anonymity you'd need to combine it with Tor or a VPN.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Can my posts be deleted?</summary>
          <p class="faq-a">You can publish a deletion event, and well-behaved relays and clients will honour it. But because anyone can archive Nostr data, you should treat posts as permanent. Think of deletion as a request, not a guarantee.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Do I need Bitcoin or Lightning to use Nostr?</summary>
          <p class="faq-a">No. Nostr and Bitcoin are independent. You can post, follow, and message without ever touching a wallet. Lightning zaps are an optional feature you can add whenever you're ready.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">What stops spam and abuse?</summary>
          <p class="faq-a">Relays set their own policies — some require a small payment or invite to post, others are open. Clients add mute/block lists and Web of Trust filtering. It's a different model to centralised moderation, and it's still maturing.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Is Nostr just for Twitter-style posts?</summary>
          <p class="faq-a">Not at all. The protocol supports long-form articles, live streams, marketplaces, Git repositories, collaborative notes, chess games, and more — all identified by event "kind" numbers. The ecosystem is growing fast.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-q">Who created Nostr?</summary>
          <p class="faq-a">The protocol was created by a pseudonymous developer known as <em>fiatjaf</em> in 2020. It gained major momentum in late 2022 when Jack Dorsey (Twitter co-founder) publicly endorsed it and donated to its development.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── FOOTER CTA ── -->
